course: dictionary
lesson: 3386
title: An outside skeleton
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Most of us have bones inside our bodies. Some animals have their skeleton on the outside instead. An exoskeleton is a hard outer covering that supports and protects the body, a bit like a suit of armour.
explain: «Insects have a hard outside skeleton called an exoskeleton.» The word is made of two parts. Exo means outside, and skeleton is the frame that holds up the body. So an exoskeleton is a skeleton on the outside.
explain: Context helps you check your meaning. The sentence says the skeleton is hard and on the outside, so an exoskeleton must be that hard outer covering. Put your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The word also appears in technology. A robotic exoskeleton is a machine suit worn on the outside of the body to help a person walk or lift heavy things. Same word, but this time it is a machine, not an animal's body.
fact: An exoskeleton is a hard outer covering that supports and protects an animal's body.
fact: Insects, spiders, crabs and lobsters have an exoskeleton instead of bones inside.
fact: Animals with bones inside their bodies have an endoskeleton.
fact: To grow, an animal must shed or moult its exoskeleton, splitting it and climbing out in a new soft one.
fact: A robotic exoskeleton is a machine suit that helps a person walk or lift heavy things.
exercise: «Insects have a hard outside skeleton called an exoskeleton.» What is an exoskeleton? | A kind of robot that cannot move | A bone inside the body | A soft new skin the animal grows | *A hard outer covering that supports and protects the body
exercise: Which animal has an exoskeleton? | A human | A dog | A horse | *A lobster
exercise: Why must an animal shed its exoskeleton? | *To grow | To eat more food | To make a noise | To find a mate
test: What does a robotic exoskeleton help a person do? | Fly over the sea | Breathe under water | *Walk or lift heavy things | Sing louder
test: Animals with bones inside their bodies have what kind of skeleton? | *An endoskeleton | An exoskeleton | A robotic skeleton | No skeleton at all
exam: Which of these is the hard outer covering of an insect? | Endoskeleton | Bone | Fur | *Exoskeleton
